        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16009897?u=175800d6f14371cdc919c42b26f9640872064761&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari supports <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/variants\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale#variants</code></a> as of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3163915252\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/issues/46992\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebKit/WebKit/pull/46992/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/46992\">WebKit/WebKit#46992</a>, which was released in <a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/releases/tag/WebKit-7622.1.21\">WebKit-622.1.21</a>, which <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/d64716cdadd87e7d87abf8206cc733d8bfcb2813/browsers/safari.json#L375\">corresponds to Safari 26</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Open Safari and paste this into the devtools:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-ts notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"new Intl.Locale('en-GB-oxendict').variants \n// should return &quot;oxendict&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Intl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">Locale</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'en-GB-oxendict'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">variants</span> \n<span class=\"pl-c\">// should return \"oxendict\"</span></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28747",
            "title": "safari 26 supports Intl.Locale#variants",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-30T06:52:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-30T06:51:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "k-yle",
                "url": "https://github.com/k-yle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24937357?u=e998536166c2ac6b9bdf5d188799dbd9f26c14e3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a note to the <code class=\"notranslate\">safari_ios</code> entry for the <code class=\"notranslate\">input.accept</code> attribute indicating that Safari iOS does not support the <code class=\"notranslate\">audio/*</code> MIME type, requiring developers to specify individual audio file extensions instead.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tested on iPad (iOS 17.0) using Safari, where setting <code class=\"notranslate\">accept=\"audio/*\"</code> does not allow picking any audio files. This behavior is documented in <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=242110\" rel=\"nofollow\">WebKit bug 242110</a>, which describes that iOS Safari treats <code class=\"notranslate\">accept=\"audio/*\"</code> identically to <code class=\"notranslate\">accept=\"video/*\"</code>, showing the video recorder and photo library options instead of audio files.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28629.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3715443817\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28629\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28629/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28629\">#28629</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28745",
            "title": "Add Safari iOS note for accept attribute audio/* limitation",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-29T15:09:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-29T15:08:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "D3SOX",
                "url": "https://github.com/D3SOX"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy: gamepad</code> appears to have been removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2364557768\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23470\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470\">#23470</a> for the reasons given in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2364557768\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23470\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470/hovercard?comment_id=2423659290&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470#issuecomment-2423659290\">#23470 (comment)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The data is definitely wierd and needs to be looked at again.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically,</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>That issues says the permission was added in 62, but in my PR of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"952418181\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/11770\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/11770/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/11770\">#11770</a> it went in at 86 behind a preference.</li>\n<li>The comment is that the feature was only supported \"on the allow iframe attribute\" based on a note that applied only to FF, so would not affect Chrome.</li>\n<li>Chrome indicate it was shipped in 103 but I can't find confirmation <a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3566388\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3566388</a></li>\n<li>Safari asserts to have supported this in tech preview 186 <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/14916/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-186/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/14916/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-186/</a> but I can't see it in <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/14205/news-from-wwdc23-webkit-features-in-safari-17-beta/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/14205/news-from-wwdc23-webkit-features-in-safari-17-beta/</a></li>\n<li>Not supported in FF, because FF only supports Feature-Policy</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/marcoscaceres/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/marcoscaceres\">@marcoscaceres</a> Do you know if this actually did release in Chrome/Safari, and if so, in what versions</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This falls out of the post <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3763982649\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42544\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42544/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42544\">mdn/content#42544</a></p>",
